  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">1. Operating Scope &amp; Legal Framework</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      Spice and Sail Zanzibar is a locally owned tour operator and private transfer specialist based at our operations hub near Mbuzini Hospital, Magharibi District, Zanzibar, Tanzania. We operate in compliance with the Zanzibar Tourism Act No. 6 of 2009. While our formal Zanzibar Commission for Tourism (ZCT) operator licence application is in process, all field excursions, private transfers, and ocean charters are fulfilled in partnership with fully certified, Zanzibari-licensed guides, vessel captains, and authorized transport providers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">2. Transparent Pricing &amp; Inclusions</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      Rates published on our website and generated by our interactive fare engines are verified catalogue planning ranges. Every booking quote provided by our reservations team is fixed and inclusive of all mandatory government taxes, guide fees, and official marine conservation levies (such as Menai Bay Marine Reserve $10 and Mnemba Marine Reserve $25). Optional personal expenses (such as museum admissions or discretionary gratuities) are explicitly itemized prior to confirmation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">3. Booking Enquiries, References &amp; Confirmation Process</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      Standard day tours (Stone Town, Spice Farm, Safari Blue, Mnemba Snorkeling, Jozani Forest) and private airport transfers require <strong>zero advance deposit</strong>. When you submit a booking request through our website or concierge, you receive an <strong>Enquiry Reference (#SP-YYYY-XXXXXX)</strong> confirming that your request is safely logged in our system. Our operations team then verifies live guide, vehicle, and vessel availability, and issues your confirmed itinerary and driver details via WhatsApp or email. You pay upon meeting your assigned private driver or guide on the day of service.
    </p>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      For multi-day packages and fly-in mainland safaris (such as Mikumi or Serengeti), flight seat confirmations apply per domestic scheduled aviation carrier terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">4. Payment Methods</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      We accept payment in cash (United States Dollars USD printed post-2009 per East African banking standards, or Tanzanian Shillings TZS at prevailing market rates), local mobile money (M-Pesa, Airtel Money, Tigo Pesa), or via secure online card payment link upon request.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">5. Safety, Marine Equipment &amp; Passenger Welfare</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      All vessels utilized for ocean activities carry marine safety gear, certified life jackets for adults and children, first-aid kits, and communication devices. All private road vehicles are licensed passenger minivans with functioning air-conditioning and seatbelts. Guests are required to follow all safety briefings from guides and vessel captains.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">6. Cultural Respect &amp; Wildlife Ethics</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      Zanzibar is a culturally rich, predominantly Muslim society. Guests are requested to dress modestly (covering shoulders and knees) when walking through Stone Town, rural villages, and local markets. In wildlife and marine environments, we enforce strict ethical rules: zero dolphin chasing, zero touching of corals or marine turtles, and mandatory safe approach distances.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">7. Statutory Insurance &amp; Liability</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      All international travelers visiting Zanzibar are required by the Revolutionary Government of Zanzibar to hold official Zanzibar Inbound Travel Insurance issued by the Zanzibar Insurance Corporation (ZIC, $44/adult). Our operations carry public passenger liability coverage. We strongly advise travelers to hold comprehensive medical and travel cancellation insurance.
    </p>
  </section>

